ntdll: let an ARM64EC process load the AMD64 binaries Wine Mono is made of.

Wine Mono's runtime is shipped as mono-2.0/bin/libmono-2.0-x86_64.dll, an
ordinary AMD64 PE that the emulator executes. is_valid_binary() compares
info->Machine against current_machine, which is IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_ARM64 in an
ARM64EC build, so the image is refused: NtCreateSection answers
STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED and open_dll_file turns it into STATUS_INVALID_IMAGE_FORMAT.
Every .NET program then dies the same way, measured on device with a 32-bit
launcher against a freshly installed runtime:

  Failed to load module L"C:\windows\mono\mono-2.0\bin\libmono-2.0-x86_64.dll";
      status=c000007b
  mscoree:load_mono Could not load Mono into this process

The check above it already makes the mirror-image exception -- ARM64EC images
inside an AMD64 process -- so the machine field alone was never the whole
question on a hybrid target.

This is deliberately separate from 0072, which installs the runtime on demand.
The two were confused once already: 0072's ancestor was deleted on the reasoning
that unbundling the .msi made the loader change pointless, which is a non
sequitur -- the relaxation is about whether Mono can be *loaded*, not about how
it arrives. Installing it on demand made the fault reappear unchanged, at the
same address, with the same status code.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
index 7091a48b7d2..3b9c323341d 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -2643,6 +2643,12 @@ static BOOL is_valid_binary( HANDLE file, const SECTION_IMAGE_INFORMATION *info
     if (NtCurrentTeb()->WowTebOffset) return TRUE;
     /* support ARM64EC binaries on x86-64 */
     if (current_machine == IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_AMD64 && has_chpe_metadata( file, info )) return TRUE;
+    /* support x86-64 binaries on ARM64EC, which is how Wine Mono arrives:
+     * mono-2.0/bin/libmono-2.0-x86_64.dll is a plain AMD64 PE and the emulator
+     * is what runs it. Without this, NtCreateSection answers STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED,
+     * open_dll_file turns that into STATUS_INVALID_IMAGE_FORMAT, and every .NET
+     * program dies on "Could not load Mono into this process" with 0xc000007b. */
+    if (current_machine == IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_ARM64 && info->Machine == IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_AMD64) return TRUE;
     /* support 32-bit IL-only images on 64-bit */
     if (!info->ImageContainsCode) return TRUE;
     if (info->ComPlusNativeReady) return TRUE;
